SECTION 3: CLEAN-ROOM C11 ARCHITECTURE & ZERO THIRD-PARTY DEPENDENCIES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
lh-kernel-preempt-patch is engineered from first principles as an independent,
clean-room C11 verification utility, jitter analysis engine, and real-time
kernel posture evaluator.

The compiled CLI utility (bin/lh-preempt) contains 100% zero third-party library
dependencies, linking exclusively against standard ISO C11 libc (POSIX.1-2008)
and the standard math library (-lm). It compiles cleanly under both GCC and Clang
with -std=c11 -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -pedantic.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 4: TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS & STANDARDS CONFORMANCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This software and patchset conforms to the following standards and frameworks:
  - ISO/IEC 9899:2011 (C11 standard)
  - Linux Kernel 6.6 LTS Real-Time Patchset (v6.6-rt)
  - POSIX.1b (Real-Time Extensions: SCHED_FIFO, SCHED_RR, mlockall, timer_create)
  - Unified Diff Format (IEEE POSIX 1003.1-2008 / patch(1))
  - Developer's Certificate of Origin (DCO 1.1)
  - OASIS SARIF v2.1.0: Static Analysis Results Interchange Format
  - OWASP & CWE Real-Time Safety Classifications:
    CWE-400 (Uncontrolled Resource Consumption / CPU Starvation),
    CWE-833 (Deadlock / Priority Inversion),
    CWE-662 (Improper Synchronization / Non-Deterministic Latency),
    CWE-667 (Improper Locking / Non-Sleeping Spinlock in RT),
    CWE-770 (Allocation of Resources Without Limits / Memory Paging Spikes),
    CWE-250 (Execution with Unnecessary Privileges / Hardware SMI Disruption),
    CWE-755 (Improper Handling of Exceptional Conditions / Missing Watchdog)
